osition": "English says rotating node 37 moves the samples of node 38 to the top; the Spanish says they move to the bottom (\"se muevan hacia abajo\").", "reader_consequence": "A Spanish reader compares the printed 'Rotated Node 37' plot with the text, sees node 38 at the top, and concludes either that ggtree::rotate() failed or that they picked the wrong node.", "confidence": "high"}, {"heading": "### Import data", "segment_index": "S5.P1", "kind": "untrue", "en_span": "chapters/phylogenetic_trees.qmd:73-73", "tr_span": "chapters/phylogenetic_trees.es.qmd:77-77", "proposition": "English says read.tree() returns a list object OF CLASS \"phylo\"; the Spanish says the object is NAMED \"phylo\" (\"un objeto tipo lista llamado \\\"phylo\\\"\"), which the adjacent chunk contradicts because the object is named tree.", "reader_consequence": "A Spanish reader looks for an object called phylo, does not find one, and loses the class name that later functions (tree_subset, ggtree) actually dispatch on.", "confidence": "medium"}, {"heading": "### Import data", "segment_index": "S5.P1", "kind": "untrue", "en_span": "chapters/phylogenetic_trees.qmd:69-69", "tr_span": "chapters/phylogenetic_trees.es.qmd:73-73", "proposition": "The example Newick string is given with decimal points in English (\"((t2:0.04,t1:0.34):0.89,...)\") but with decimal commas in Spanish (\"((t2:0,04,t1:0,34):0,89,...)\"), so the Spanish example is not a valid Newick string.", "reader_consequence": "A Spanish reader takes the shown string as the Newick standard and writes or edits a .nwk file with decimal commas, which ape::read.tree() cannot parse because the comma is the Newick node separator.", "confidence": "medium"}, {"heading": "## More complex trees: adding heatmaps of sample data", "segment_index": "S16.P11", "kind": "added", "en_span": "chapters/phylogenetic_trees.qmd:611-611", "tr_span": "chapters/phylogenetic_trees.es.qmd:625-625", "proposition": "The Spanish states that the extra colour layer represents the genes conferring antimicrobial resistance (\"otra capa de colores representando los genes que confieren resistencia antimicrobiana\"); the English says only \"another color scheme layer\".", "reader_consequence": "A Spanish reader may expect the new colour scale itself to encode resistance genes, when new_scale_fill() only frees the fill aesthetic and the gene variable is supplied by the following gheatmap() call.", "confidence": "low"}]}